  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-source-ledger",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-source-ledger) [](LICENSE)\n\n> Author: jetpan (npm) ↔ jerentpan-lab (GitHub) | [npm package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-source-ledger) | [GitHub repo](https://github.com/jerentpan-lab/dsh-source-ledger) | install from GitHub: `dsh plugin --profile web add github:jerentpan-lab/dsh-source-ledger`"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-source-ledger",
      "text": "Decision-grade claims must carry an inspectable **source pointer** (url / `file:line` /\nmessage id). Claims without one are flagged `[no-source]` and cannot be verified.\n`source_audit` reports the source-tag rate and returns a random sample for independent\nrecomputation.\n\nMotivation: agents drift when the same fact has two executable sources. \"Outside the\nsession / without a source, it is not a fact.\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-source-ledger\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "- `source_assert { claim, source?, owner?, recompute? }`\n- `source_verify { id, note? }` — only works when a source exists\n- `source_audit { sampleN? }` — source rate + random sample\n- `source_list { onlyMissingSource? }`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Config (0.2.0)",
      "text": "```json\n{ \"ledgerFile\": \"~/.dsh/source-ledger.jsonl\" }\n```\n\n- `ledgerFile`: append-only ledger path (default `~/.dsh/source-ledger.jsonl`, env `DSH_SOURCE_LEDGER_FILE`).\n- Unknown keys / invalid values throw a readable `ConfigError`.\n- Example: `config.example.json`. Run `npm run verify` for tests + pack checks."
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "```bash\nnode examples/demo.mjs\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Bench",
      "text": "`node bench/bench.mjs` writes `bench/RESULTS.md` (this host: 1000 entries+audit p50 ≈ 3.0ms, 10000 ≈ 17.2ms)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting (error table)",
      "text": "| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ConfigError ... unknown key` | typo/unsupported config key | use `config.example.json` |\n| `ConfigError ... pointerTypes` | unknown pointer type | allowed: url, file, file-line, message, commit, stdout |\n| `source_assert: claim is required` | empty claim | pass a claim |\n| `verify: entry ... has no inspectable pointer` | weak/none source | assert with a pointer type |\n| `source changed since assert` | file/url content hash differs | re-assert with the new content |\n| `source unreachable` | source file/url missing | restore source or re-assert |\n| `source_verify: id is required` | missing id | pass an entry id |\n| `report` not written | bad outFile path | use an absolute writable path |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Verify",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm run verify\n```"
    },
    {
